WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:03.980
Is a nifty little device that was created

2
00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:11.740
specifically for the Singer/ Studio SK 150
and SK 151 bulky machines.

3
00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:17.500
It's a 12 stitch repeat pattern selector to
make quick work of using punch cards

4
00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:22.380
on a manual machine without
a built in punch card mechanism.

5
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.200
If you are lucky enough to find one

6
00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:31.320
of these rare devices, it could also
work for any 9 millimeter bulky machine.

7
00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.320
It consists of the pattern selector

8
00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:38.140
device, a needle selector, card snaps,
punch cards,

9
00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:42.560
and it originally came with a unique
number strip for the needle bed that was

10
00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:47.620
marked for sets of 12
repeats of the needles.

11
00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:53.100
As long as you have these pieces, you
can use this without the number strip.

12
00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:55.440
The pattern selector has slots that are

13
00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:59.740
designed to fit over the screw
heads on a Silver machine.

14
00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:02.420
I'm not showing an SK-150 here,

15
00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:08.660
but the screw heads happen to be the same
and I can mount the device on the machine.

16
00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:10.800
The device slips over the screw heads.

17
00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:14.050
There's no need to adjust them.

18
00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:16.700
The original punch cards were fairly long,

19
00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:21.050
long enough to go through the device so
the ends could be snapped together

20
00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:25.840
and the card made into a loop
for continuous knitting.

21
00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:27.560
With the printed side down,

22
00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:31.660
feed one end of the card
into the lower part of the slot.

23
00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:33.900
Once it's moved a few inches through,

24
00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:40.800
loop the card and feed the other end
into the upper slot until it catches.

25
00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:44.320
Then carefully turn the knob,

26
00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:48.700
advancing the end of the card
that is in the upper slot.

27
00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:53.900
Keep turning until you can
join the two ends into a loop.

28
00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:58.180
Line up the ends and join
them with the card snaps.

29
00:01:58.210 --> 00:02:02.060
I'm using a long piece of blank
cardstock as an example.

30
00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:05.360
I don't have the original cards.

31
00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:16.500
Once the loop is formed,
position the card to look like this.

32
00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:17.660
Now, be careful.

33
00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:24.100
I discovered that the Toyota 12 stitch
repeat cards do not fit in this device.

34
00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:28.580
The holes are not positioned
to the same and they will not work.

35
00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:32.800
Be sure you have Studio/
Singer 12 stitch cards.

36
00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.380
Be sure the cards overlap correctly so

37
00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:41.920
they don't jam as you cycle
it through the device.

38
00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:47.920
Position the stitch pattern so
the row you want to knit is on top.

39
00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:53.260
Push the reset button so the fingers
of the needle selector are aligned.

40
00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:55.700
Then with the A side of the needle

41
00:02:55.730 --> 00:03:01.920
selector facing you, push the fingers
into the pattern slot to select needles.

42
00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:04.840
Rise the needle pusher and notice how some

43
00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:08.440
of the fingers are
in out of work position.

44
00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.680
Using the working fingers as you would any

45
00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:15.860
other needle selector,
pull needles out to D position.

46
00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:19.520
Repeat this across the row
for your stitch pattern.

47
00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:22.000
This is where the special number strip

48
00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:27.400
would come in handy, making it
easier to see groups of 12 needles.

49
00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:29.640
When all the needles have been selected

50
00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:34.420
and the carriage is set for patterning,
knit across the row.

51
00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:40.760
For the next pattern row, push the reset
button again and advance the card.

52
00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:43.440
Repeat selecting the fingers of the needle

53
00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:48.340
selector and selecting the new
needles across the row.

54
00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:51.140
Remember, this device
is completely manual.

55
00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:53.500
You need to reset the needle pusher,

56
00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:59.900
advance the card, and reselect the fingers
of the needle pusher for each row.

57
00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:02.140
Even though this is a manual device,

58
00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:08.080
it can make selecting needles a whole lot
easier and faster with these machines.

